Files: docs/models.js, docs/app.js, tests/web/browser_smoke.mjs, tests/web/run_browser_smoke.sh, README.md.
No change needed in: docs/worker.js, docs/index.html (the warn style already exists), docs/refine.js, tests/web/refine.test.mjs (it does not import models.js).

The same diff is saved at /tmp/claude-1000/-home-abel-claude-AlphaMaker/e817cea6-a82c-4d1c-95c9-48c35fff1559/scratchpad/proposal.diff and it passes `git apply --check`. The script that generates it is /tmp/claude-1000/-home-abel-claude-AlphaMaker/e817cea6-a82c-4d1c-95c9-48c35fff1559/scratchpad/make_proposal.py. The scratchpad can be cleared, so the full text is below.

How it covers the four requirements:
- (a) New entry 'isnet-general', listed first, so it is also the fallback. It is the default on both backends. The URL is pinned and byte-identical to the benchmarked file. Preprocessing is the same as core.py: 1024, HALF, minmax. The same fp32 file is used for wasm and webgpu.
- (b) The RMBG menu labels now say "(niet voor commercieel gebruik)". The licence line now says "...Dit model mag niet commercieel gebruikt worden; kies daarvoor een ander model of neem een licentie bij Bria." in red and bold. Because the label is reused by the worker, the loading/downloading/starting lines show the warning too. After every photo the status line adds "Let op: gemaakt met RMBG-1.4 (niet voor commercieel gebruik)."
- (c) The "Nauwkeurig:" and "Licht:" framing is gone; the default is labelled "IS-Net general (standaard)".
- (d) With no model argument, the smoke test now uses whatever the page preselects. It fails unless the licence line starts with MIT, Apache-2.0 or BSD. `run_browser_smoke.sh '' rmbg-1.4-licht` still tests RMBG.

What the menu looks like after the change (simulated):
- WASM: IS-Net general (standaard) · 170 MB (selected; "Licentie: Apache-2.0"), (disabled) BiRefNet lite, RMBG-1.4 (niet voor commercieel gebruik) · 168 MB, RMBG-1.4 licht (niet voor commercieel gebruik) · 42 MB, (disabled) BEN2, (disabled) BiRefNet.
- WebGPU: the same list with everything enabled; RMBG-1.4 is 84 MB there.

